# PHP App Conventions

## New files in `app/`

- Start with `declare(strict_types=1);`
- Use scalar type hints and return types on all public methods
- Services must not type-hint HTTP `Request`; use validated arrays + context arrays

## Structure

- `app/Http/Controllers/{Domain}/` — thin controllers only
- `app/Http/Requests/{Domain}/` — validation only (`rules`, `messages`, `authorize`, `withValidator`)
- `app/Services/{Domain}/` — one domain service per aggregate
- `app/Facades/` — only for singleton services registered in `AppServiceProvider`

## Tests

- Feature tests hit real named routes (`route('login')`), not controller internals
- Assert redirects, session, and database side-effects

## Style

- Follow Laravel Pint / project style; do not introduce a second formatting style
- Prefer constructor injection in controllers; Facade calls are acceptable for domain services
